        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Ho Chi Minh</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1890 CE – 1969 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">19 May 1890 (the generally accepted date; he also gave 1891, 1892, 1894 and 1895) in the village of Hoàng Trù, Kim Liên commune, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nghe-an-province">Nghệ An province</a>, as Nguyễn Sinh Cung; son of Nguyễn Sinh Sắc, a Confucian scholar and teacher, later an imperial magistrate</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">2 September 1969, of heart failure, at his home in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a>, aged 79; embalmed and displayed in a mausoleum in Ba Đình Square, against his wish to be cremated</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Founding member of the French Communist Party (1920); <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-international">Comintern</a> agent; founder of the Vietnamese Revolutionary Youth League (1925) and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochinese-communist-party">Indochinese Communist Party</a> (1930); leader of the Việt Minh (from 1941); prime minister (1945–1955) and president (1946–1969) of the Democratic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>; party chairman until his death</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">the Việt Minh and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/august-revolution">August Revolution</a>; the Declaration of Independence of the Democratic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> (1945); the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-indochina-war">First Indochina War</a> and Điện Biên Phủ; the land reform of 1953–1956 and its executions; the Hồ Chí Minh trail; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam-war">Vietnam War</a>; the name &quot;Uncle Ho&quot;; his poems, among them the Prison Diary</span></div>
