    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Born Nguyễn Sinh Cung in Annam, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">French Indochina</a>, Hồ Chí Minh left in 1911 as a ship's kitchen helper and spent three decades abroad, becoming a founding member of the French Communist Party, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-international">Comintern</a> agent and in 1930 founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochinese-communist-party">Indochinese Communist Party</a>.</li><li>Returning in 1941, he led the Việt Minh, proclaimed the Democratic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> in 1945 and fought the French until their defeat at Điện Biên Phủ in 1954, after which he ruled North Vietnam as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/one-party-state">one-party state</a>.</li><li>His government suppressed rival nationalists and carried out a land reform with executions whose number historians still dispute; he backed the insurgency in the South through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam-war">Vietnam War</a> and died in 1969, six years before North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> won it.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Hồ is known to have used between 50 and 200 pseudonyms. He began regularly using the name Hồ Chí Minh, &quot;Bright spirit&quot; or &quot;Clear will&quot;, only after his release from a Chinese prison in 1943.</p></aside>
    </section>

